      "writtenOn": "2017-04-28T03:29:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Or we can have a table of recovery buttons defined by the board and handle the check here in button.c.\n\nEvery board using CONFIG_BUTTON_RECOVERY will have to define a table like:\nconst struct button_config *recovery_buttons[] \u003d {\n \u0026buttons[BUTTON_VOLUME_DOWN],\n \u0026buttons[BUTTON_VOLUME_UP],\n};\n\nconst uint8_t recovery_buttons_count \u003d ARRAY_SIZE(recovery_buttons);\n\nand button.c can implement something like:\n\nint is_recovery_mode_requested(void)\n{\n     uint8_t i;\n    for (i \u003d 0; i \u003c recovery_buttons_count; i++) {\n          if (!raw_button_pressed(recovery_buttons[i]))\n                 return 0;\n   }\n   return 1;\n}\n\nThat way we can allow any number of buttons to be used by the boards and have minimal overhead for checking recovery mode.\n\nThoughts?",
